<title>USA: State Fin'l votes 6-for-5 split, div hike.</title>
<headline>State Fin'l votes 6-for-5 split, div hike.</headline>
<dateline>HALES CORNERS, Wis. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Financial Services Corp said Tuesday it voted a six-for-five stock split and will retain its current $0.12 a share cash dividend following the split, effecting a 20 percent increase to the quarterly payout.</p>
<p>The additional shares will be issued February 28, record February 14. The cash dividend will be paid April 7, record March 24.</p>
<p>State Financial is a bank holding company.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
